  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Check account, mailbox usage, and devices per KB-009"
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I looked into this. Your mailbox is healthy and well under its size limit, and your laptop is online and connected to our systems. Since your phone is getting all your mail, the problem is with Outlook on the laptop, not your mailbox. Please try these steps in order and stop once mail starts coming in: 1) Close Outlook completely and open it again. 2) Go to the Send / Receive tab and check whether 'Work Offline' is highlighted. If it is, click it to turn it off. 3) Restart your laptop. 4) If it's still stuck, sign in to Outlook on the web. If you see your new mail there, reply to this ticket and we'll help you rebuild your Outlook profile, which makes Outlook download your mailbox again. If new mail is missing on the web too, please tell us right away so we can send this to our senior team.",
  "internal_note": "VIP user (CEO). P3, Outlook desktop not syncing since this morning, mobile fine. Followed KB-009 quick checks: mailbox 17.4% used (8.9/50 GB), so not a quota issue (KB-010 ruled out). Laptop BL-LT-0101 is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:53 UTC, 60% disk free, no warnings. Account active, no lockout. Mobile sync working points to a client-side problem. Sent the user KB-009 fix steps: restart Outlook, turn off Work Offline, reboot, then profile rebuild. Asked her to check Outlook on the web. Escalate per KB-009 if mail is missing on the web too or other users report the same thing. Since she's VIP, consider following up proactively if she hasn't replied.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
